# This copy keeps the aten semantics but restructures the launch:
# - holdable shapes (whole channel fits two fp32 tiles) run one program per
#   channel with a single load set feeding both the reduction and the
#   elementwise pass (2R+1W instead of 3R+1W traffic);
# - larger shapes split the batch rows across (channel, row-block) groups so
#   the grid fills the device, with an affine spatial loop inside each group
#   (probe: task-per-tile variants without the inner loop lose pipelining and
#   run at half the per-program streaming rate). The reduction stage stores
#   one joined [term1, term2] vector per group through a single tree call
#   (probe: each tl.sum costs a fixed ~1.6 us on this backend), and the apply
#   stage combines the per-channel group partials in two small trees.
